H-ROAD: q-twist (state relabel e->q*e) and the slope-band link to HYP-2703
==========================================================================
   s | rotation reset t*(s) | bandcover_s(consec_8)
   0 |        None          |   0.14286
   1 |           7          |   0.30952
   2 |           7          |   0.42381
   3 |           7          |   0.30952
   4 |           7          |   0.40476
   5 |           7          |   0.41429
   6 |           7          |   0.28571
   HONEST CORRECTION: pure-rotation skeleton {s*e mod7: e=0..7} is FULL
   (=Z/7) for ALL s with gcd(s,7)=1 (s=1..6); only s=0 is degenerate {0}.
   So 'rotation reset length' is 7 for every s>=1 and does NOT distinguish
   the bands. The slow-band loss at s=1 (HYP-2703 R1) is therefore NOT
   explained by rotation speed -- the q-twist is a clean state relabel but
   the per-band extremality failure is a Sturmian floor-spread effect, not
   a synchronization-speed effect. The road-coloring reset DOES cleanly
   explain s=0 (degenerate road: coverage impossible from rotation alone).

