VERDICT: PARTIAL. The genuine automaton is the 2-letter rotation (L=+q,
H=+q+1) Sturmian road on Z/7. Rotations are PERMUTATIONS so it is NEVER
synchronizing in Cerny's state-collapse sense; the LRC notion is COVERAGE
(reachability fullness), not synchronization. The lasting YIELD is the
PROVED span-domination lemma: measS7(E) <= measS7(consec_{max(E)+1}),
a pointwise tautology (visited set is monotone under adding probes). But
it does NOT close the fixed-cardinality crux. Road-coloring cleanly
explains only the degenerate band s=0. NET: clean PARTIAL + sharp DEAD-END
for synchronization as a NEW certificate.
